From: campaign 2
Subject: [PATCH] perception: gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview was retired mid-campaign

TiPToP hardcodes the Gemini model it grounds objects with. The pinned value,
`gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview`, stopped resolving on 2026-08-31 at 01:23 local:

    404 NOT_FOUND. models/gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview is not found for API
    version v1beta, or is not supported for generateContent.

Effect: 57.5% of planning requests failed at the perception step, and TiPToP's
Pick-v1.5 cell scored 41.9% against a leaderboard 67.5%. Exactly the shape of
campaign 1's M2T2 outage -- a dependent service returning well-formed failures that
read as poor policy performance rather than as an outage. Campaign 1 measured 64%
on this cell on 2026-08-18, when the preview model still existed.

`gemini-robotics-er-2-preview` is the successor and is present in the account's
model list; verified with a live generateContent call before applying.

Note the failure mode this makes explicit: a hardcoded *preview* model id is a
dependency that can be withdrawn without notice, mid-run, and the resulting scores
look like a policy problem. Worth a startup health check if TiPToP is run again.

Base commit: d8f5afdaa94a7432220c3042f9f80be5ab45aae8
